{"name":"Blush Hour","hex":"#ff6f91","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of blushing; a pink or red glow on the face caused by embarrassment, shame, shyness, love, etc.","A glow; a flush of colour, especially pink or red."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become red or pink in the face (and sometimes experience an associated feeling of warmth), especially due to shyness, love, shame, excitement, or embarrassment.","To be shy, ashamed, or embarrassed (to do something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blush"},{"term":"hour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A unit of time of one twenty-fourth of a day (sixty minutes).","A season, moment, or time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blush (Kevin Abstract album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blush is the fifth studio album by American rapper Kevin Abstract, released on June 27, 2025, through Virgin Records, X8, and Abstract's label Juno. Although marketed as Abstract's fifth solo album, the project sees Abstract take on a curation role, with the album featuring a multitude of collaborators. Abstract himself does not appear on every track."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Kevin_Abstract_-_Blush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blush_(Kevin_Abstract_album)","wikidata":"Q135012763"},{"title":"Blush (Asian band)","blocks":[{"text":"Blush was a Hong Kong–based Asian girl group originally composed of five members from the Philippines, India, China, Japan, and South Korea. They were formed by FarWest Entertainment in 2010 with the intent of popularizing an Asian vocal act in the United States as well as in all of Asia. They perform in the English language and the members currently reside in Los Angeles, California. A reality show called Project Lotus: The Search for Blush about how the band was formed premiered on Channel V on March 8, 2012. They were the first Asian group to have its debut single hit the top 3 on a major US Billboard chart when \"Undivided\" featuring Snoop Dogg reached No. 3 on the Billboard Dance/Play Chart. Their second single, \"Dance On\", reached No. 1 on that chart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Blush_Band_on_RealTVfilms.jpg/330px-Blush_Band_on_RealTVfilms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blush_(Asian_band)","wikidata":"Q196696"},{"title":"Hour","blocks":[{"text":"An hour is a unit of time historically reckoned as 1⁄24 of a day and defined contemporarily as exactly 3,600 seconds. There are 60 minutes in an hour, and 24 hours in a day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif/330px-AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hour","wikidata":"Q25235"},{"title":"Blush (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Blush is a medium bright tone of pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Blush_rose_1.jpg/330px-Blush_rose_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blush_(color)","wikidata":"Q22133966"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9d/Make_You_Blush_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9d/Make_You_Blush_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Make You Blush album cover.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMake_You_Blush_album_cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/DigitalClock_1hour.gif/500px-DigitalClock_1hour.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/DigitalClock_1hour.gif/500px-DigitalClock_1hour.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Midnight to 1 a.m. on a 24-hour clock with a digital face","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADigitalClock_1hour.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Bishopstone_sundial.jpg/500px-Bishopstone_sundial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Bishopstone_sundial.jpg/500px-Bishopstone_sundial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 7th-century Saxon tide dial on the porch at Bishopstone in Sussex, with larger crosses marking the canonical hours.[18]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABishopstone_sundial.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif/330px-Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif/330px-Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Top view of an equatorial sundial. The hour lines are spaced equally about the circle, and the shadow of the gnomon (a thin cylindrical rod) rotates uniformly. The height of the gnomon is 5⁄12 the outer radius of the dial. This animation depicts the motion of the shadow from 3 a.m. to 9 p.m. on mid-summer's day, when the Sun is at its highest declination (roughly 23.5°). Sunrise and sunset occur at 3 a.m. and 9 p.m. respectively on that day at geographical latitudes near 57.5°, roughly the latitude of Aberdeen or Sitka, Alaska.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEquatorial_sundial_topview.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Planispheric_astrolabe.png/500px-Planispheric_astrolabe.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Planispheric_astrolabe.png/500px-Planispheric_astrolabe.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Planispheric astrolabe designed for the latitude of Varese (Italy)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlanispheric_astrolabe.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/AstiCattedrale.jpg/500px-AstiCattedrale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/AstiCattedrale.jpg/500px-AstiCattedrale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sundial with Italian hours in Asti","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAstiCattedrale.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Clock_Tower_from_Su_Song%27s_Book.JPG/500px-Clock_Tower_from_Su_Song%27s_Book.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Clock_Tower_from_Su_Song%27s_Book.JPG/500px-Clock_Tower_from_Su_Song%27s_Book.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Chinese diagram from Su Song's AD 1092 Xinyi Xiangfa Yao illustrating his clocktower at Kaifeng.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClock_Tower_from_Su_Song's_Book.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Beijing_2006_1-14.jpg/500px-Beijing_2006_1-14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Beijing_2006_1-14.jpg/1280px-Beijing_2006_1-14.jpg